    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nvisual mode motions from `normal!` don't create selection for each cursor\n\nExample:\n<img width=\"50\" height=\"65\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8f673748-f4b7-4f1b-9a1e-692e9de670b1\" />\n\nrelated: #41606 \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim --clean`\n2. insert some text:\n```\nfoo\nbar\n```\n3. press `gg0QjQ1q=` in normal mode\n4. run `:normal! viw`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nEach cursor should have its own visual selection:\n\n<img width=\"48\" height=\"59\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f8ce1328-0dab-4a83-b6ee-8e56f3665046\" />\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1522+g b21f2094ba Build type: Release LuaJIT 2.1.1788460057\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nN/A\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.40.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from source",
