        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Can you elaborate the acutla use-case here? generally `:norm!` is not considered user (interactive) input. \n\nI suppose a case can be made that an interactive `:...` cmdline typed by the user is user-input. But we need to be clear about whether all such commands should attempt to cascade to multicursors, or not.\n\nMeanwhile, it is somewhat easy to cascade the Visual-only case:\n\n    :normal! viw\n\nbut ~~it is an open question about what should happen~~ if the operation is completed (does _not_ cascade):\n\n    :normal! viwd",
